From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Badis Meddouri <meddouri.badis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: bail out of KeyguardViewMediator#handleShow when
 there is no keyguard

On Android TV there is no keyguard: CentralSurfaces is never instantiated, so
the notification shade, StatusBarKeyguardViewManager and the keyguard view all
stay null.

PhoneWindowManager.systemReady() nevertheless routes into KeyguardService and
then onSystemReady() -> doKeyguardLocked() -> showLocked(), which posts SHOW to
the mediator's handler. handleShow() then dereferences those phone-only objects
and NPEs on the SystemUI main thread, so SystemUI crash-loops from early boot
and the screen stays black: FallbackHome is the focused activity, but its window
never receives a surface (mHasSurface=false isReadyForDisplay()=false), so
screencap returns an all-black frame.

The NPEs surface one at a time as each layer is reached:

  #00 StatusBarKeyguardViewManager.reset -> NotificationPanelViewController.resetViews
  #00 ShadeControllerImpl.instantCollapseShade -> NotificationPanelViewController.instantCollapse

Guarding handleShow() on mCentralSurfaces short-circuits all of them at the
entry point instead of patching each call site. This follows the existing
null-CentralSurfaces guard in StatusBarKeyguardViewManager, and the lazy
mShowKeyguardWakeLock creation in the previous patch (showLocked() runs before
handleShow() and needs the wake lock either way).

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
@@ -2558,6 +2558,15 @@ public class KeyguardViewMediator implements RemoteInputController.Callback
                 if (DEBUG) Log.d(TAG, "handleShow");
             }
 
+            // On devices without a keyguard (Android TV) there is no CentralSurfaces
+            // and therefore no notification shade, no StatusBarKeyguardViewManager and
+            // no keyguard view. Everything below reaches into those and NPEs on the
+            // main thread, crash-looping SystemUI and leaving a black screen. There is
+            // nothing to show, so return instead of dereferencing them.
+            if (mCentralSurfaces == null) {
+                if (DEBUG) Log.d(TAG, "ignoring handleShow, no keyguard on this device.");
+                return;
+            }
+
             mKeyguardExitAnimationRunner = null;
             mWakeAndUnlocking = false;
             setPendingLock(false);
